  "source": "{\"main.blocks\": \"<xml xmlns=\\\"https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml\\\"></xml>\", \"main.ts\": \"// SUDO for Minecraft \\u2014 now with target SELECTORS\\n//\\n// TARGET can be a selector instead of a fixed name:\\n//   @p              nearest player\\n//   @r              a random player\\n//   @a              all players\\n//   @a[name=\\\"Bob\\\"]  a specific player by name\\n//\\n// ACTION = the command they run (leave OFF the leading slash)\\nlet TARGET = \\\"@r\\\"\\nlet ACTION = \\\"say Hello everyone \\u2014 I am totally doing this myself.\\\"\\n\\n// \\\"sudo\\\" forces the targeted player(s) to actually run ACTION.\\nplayer.onChat(\\\"sudo\\\", function () {\\n    player.execute(`execute as ${TARGET} at @s run ${ACTION}`)\\n})\\n\\n// \\\"fakechat\\\" just makes chat LOOK like the target said ACTION.\\n// The {\\\"selector\\\": ...} part pulls in the real player's name.\\nplayer.onChat(\\\"fakechat\\\", function () {\\n    player.execute(`tellraw @a {\\\"rawtext\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"<\\\"},{\\\"selector\\\":\\\"${TARGET}\\\"},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"> ${ACTION}\\\"}]}`)\\n})\\n\", \"README.md\": \"# Sudo (with selectors)\\n\\n`TARGET` accepts a selector: `@p` nearest, `@r` random, `@a` all,\\nor `@a[name=\\\"Bob\\\"]` for a specific player.\\n\\n- Type **sudo** in chat: forces the target to actually run `ACTION` (`execute as`).\\n- Type **fakechat** in chat: makes a chat line look like the target said `ACTION`.\\n\\nEdit `TARGET` and `ACTION` at the top of the code.\\n\", \"pxt.json\": \"{\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"sudo\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Force a player (by selector) to run a command, or fake their chat.\\\",\\n    \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n        \\\"core\\\": \\\"*\\\",\\n        \\\"minecraft\\\": \\\"*\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"files\\\": [\\n        \\\"main.blocks\\\",\\n        \\\"main.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"README.md\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"preferredEditor\\\": \\\"tsprj\\\"\\n}\"}"
}